WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:02.335
This is CNN breaking news.

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:03.403
We have major

00:00:03.403 --> 00:00:05.038
breaking news, indeed, historic

00:00:05.038 --> 00:00:06.106
breaking news right now.

00:00:06.106 --> 00:00:06.406
CNN's

00:00:06.406 --> 00:00:08.008
Kara Scannell is in New York

00:00:08.008 --> 00:00:09.476
for us covering this story.

00:00:09.476 --> 00:00:12.145
What are you learning, Kara?

00:00:12.712 --> 00:00:14.080
Well, Wolf, three sources

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:15.181
tell me and my colleague

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:16.850
John Miller that a manhattan grand

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:19.185
jury has indicted former President

00:00:19.185 --> 00:00:20.887
Donald Trump in connection

00:00:20.887 --> 00:00:22.789
with the hush money payment scheme.

00:00:22.789 --> 00:00:24.357
This indictment is under seal,

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:25.525
according to sources,

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:26.659
and the exact charges

00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:28.862
are not yet known at this time.

00:00:28.862 --> 00:00:30.330
But this investigation

00:00:30.330 --> 00:00:32.132
has been going on for a long time.

00:00:32.132 --> 00:00:34.067
The decision to move and seek

00:00:34.067 --> 00:00:35.468
and get an indictment

00:00:35.468 --> 00:00:36.036
of a former

00:00:36.036 --> 00:00:37.470
president is the first time

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:39.572
that has been done in U.S. history.

00:00:39.773 --> 00:00:41.508
This could have a significant impact

00:00:41.508 --> 00:00:43.576
on the presidential campaign.

00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:45.345
But as as I said, we do not know

00:00:45.345 --> 00:00:46.479
the exact charges yet.

00:00:46.479 --> 00:00:48.782
We expect those charges to be made public

00:00:49.015 --> 00:00:50.150
in the coming days.

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:52.285
And at some point in the near future,

00:00:52.285 --> 00:00:53.019
former President

00:00:53.019 --> 00:00:54.287
Trump will have to come to

00:00:54.287 --> 00:00:56.823
this courthouse and be arraigned Wolf.

00:00:56.823 --> 00:00:58.725
The grand jury did meet today,

00:00:58.725 --> 00:00:59.793
even though they're

00:00:59.793 --> 00:01:01.127
taking a break next week

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:02.662
and for a few weeks thereafter.

00:01:02.662 --> 00:01:04.731
They did meet today and presumably

00:01:04.731 --> 00:01:06.366
they could have voted on this indictment

00:01:06.366 --> 00:01:09.135
today, is that right?

00:01:09.569 --> 00:01:10.370
Yeah, Wolf,

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:12.005
according to my colleagues,

00:01:12.005 --> 00:01:13.373
we have observed prosecutors

00:01:13.373 --> 00:01:14.474
going into the room

00:01:14.474 --> 00:01:16.676
where the grand jury meets.

00:01:16.676 --> 00:01:17.710
They were meeting today.

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:18.211
We were told

00:01:18.211 --> 00:01:19.145
it was not scheduled

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:20.513
to hear any testimony

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:22.048
on the Trump investigation,

00:01:22.048 --> 00:01:23.083
but they have been working

00:01:23.083 --> 00:01:24.384
diligently since January,

00:01:24.384 --> 00:01:25.819
hearing witness testimony.

00:01:25.819 --> 00:01:27.921
And it is up to prosecutors to decide

00:01:28.054 --> 00:01:28.755
if they were going

00:01:28.755 --> 00:01:29.923
to move forward in indictment

00:01:29.923 --> 00:01:32.292
and when to ask that grand jury to vote.

00:01:32.392 --> 00:01:33.460
It appears they went in

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:35.028
and asked them to vote today

00:01:35.028 --> 00:01:36.062
and that they were in there

00:01:36.062 --> 00:01:37.230
late this afternoon.

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:39.432
This grand jury meets until 5 p.m..

00:01:39.566 --> 00:01:41.835
It appears as though this vote came down

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:43.103
just in the past

00:01:43.103 --> 00:01:43.937
couple of minutes,

00:01:43.937 --> 00:01:45.405
within the last hour Wolf.

00:01:45.405 --> 00:01:47.073
Very dramatic development indeed.

00:01:47.073 --> 00:01:48.441
The first time, as you say,

00:01:48.441 --> 00:01:49.542
in American history,

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:51.277
that a former president

00:01:51.277 --> 00:01:52.078
of the United States

00:01:52.078 --> 00:01:53.680
has been formally indicted

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:55.381
in a criminal investigation.

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:56.449
Let's go to our senior

00:01:56.449 --> 00:01:58.318
legal affairs correspondent, Paula Reid,

00:01:58.318 --> 00:01:59.953
who's also following these developments.

00:01:59.953 --> 00:02:01.221
What else are you learning?

00:02:01.221 --> 00:02:02.222
Wolf, I'm actually texting

00:02:02.222 --> 00:02:02.956
with one of the former

00:02:02.956 --> 00:02:04.924
president's attorneys right now.

00:02:04.924 --> 00:02:05.892
As of several minutes ago,

00:02:05.892 --> 00:02:07.727
they had not been told by prosecutors

00:02:07.727 --> 00:02:09.229
about this indictment,

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:10.497
but we're talking about conduct

00:02:10.497 --> 00:02:12.265
that occurred about seven years ago.

00:02:12.265 --> 00:02:13.700
This has been under investigation

00:02:13.700 --> 00:02:15.902
for approximately five years.

00:02:15.902 --> 00:02:17.270
But in recent months,

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:18.905
this investigation has heated up

00:02:18.905 --> 00:02:19.672
once again.

00:02:19.672 --> 00:02:21.641
We've seen a parade of high profile

00:02:21.641 --> 00:02:22.575
witnesses, close

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:24.477
associates of the former president

00:02:24.477 --> 00:02:26.779
going before the grand jury to testify.

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:28.581
And there was anticipation

00:02:28.581 --> 00:02:29.682
that this investigation

00:02:29.682 --> 00:02:31.451
was finally coming to an end.

00:02:31.451 --> 00:02:32.051
And as Kara

00:02:32.051 --> 00:02:32.485
and John

00:02:32.485 --> 00:02:33.353
just reported,

00:02:33.353 --> 00:02:33.653
Piers,

00:02:33.653 --> 00:02:36.489
the grand jury has voted to indict.

00:02:36.789 --> 00:02:37.891
Now, the district attorney

00:02:37.891 --> 00:02:39.092
has been under some pressure.

00:02:39.092 --> 00:02:40.960
He has been criticized for

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:42.829
by some for not pursuing

00:02:42.829 --> 00:02:43.897
this more aggressively.

00:02:43.897 --> 00:02:45.198
And then when this investigation

00:02:45.198 --> 00:02:46.266
heated up again,

00:02:46.266 --> 00:02:47.367
some people questioned

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:48.801
whether he should go ahead

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:49.936
with this, arguing

00:02:49.936 --> 00:02:50.703
that this was

00:02:50.703 --> 00:02:51.638
not one of the more

00:02:51.638 --> 00:02:53.106
significant investigations

00:02:53.106 --> 00:02:54.707
the former president would face.

00:02:54.707 --> 00:02:55.675
But clearly today,

00:02:55.675 --> 00:02:57.510
they move forward with the grand jury

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:58.945
to get an indictment,

00:02:58.945 --> 00:03:00.413
as it has been explained to us

00:03:00.413 --> 00:03:01.915
by the DA's office.

00:03:01.915 --> 00:03:02.682
What will happen

00:03:02.682 --> 00:03:03.116
next is

00:03:03.116 --> 00:03:05.451
that is expected to be filed under seal,

00:03:05.652 --> 00:03:07.320
and then they will have to negotiate

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:08.755
a self surrender

00:03:08.755 --> 00:03:10.390
from the former president.

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:11.791
Now, we've been told by his legal team

00:03:11.791 --> 00:03:14.027
that he is expected to fully cooperate.

00:03:14.194 --> 00:03:15.795
And the last time we spoke to them,

00:03:15.795 --> 00:03:17.297
it appeared that the former president

00:03:17.297 --> 00:03:19.732
absolutely wanted to appear in person

00:03:19.732 --> 00:03:22.202
and fully participate in the process

00:03:22.502 --> 00:03:23.703
of being fingerprinted,

00:03:23.703 --> 00:03:24.737
photographed,

00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:25.838
going before a judge

00:03:25.838 --> 00:03:27.640
as any other citizen would.

00:03:27.640 --> 00:03:28.441
The former president

00:03:28.441 --> 00:03:29.542
appears to believe

00:03:29.542 --> 00:03:30.243
that this is

00:03:30.243 --> 00:03:32.278
an advantageous thing for him

00:03:32.278 --> 00:03:33.112
politically.

00:03:33.112 --> 00:03:34.180
So it'll be interesting

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:34.547
to see

00:03:34.547 --> 00:03:35.782
what the terms of this self

00:03:35.782 --> 00:03:37.684
surrender are.

00:03:37.684 --> 00:03:39.819
So so he would have to actually show up

00:03:39.819 --> 00:03:40.687
and be fingerprinted

00:03:40.687 --> 00:03:42.822
and go through that entire process

00:03:42.822 --> 00:03:44.390
like any normal U.S.

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:46.426
citizen would have to go through

00:03:46.426 --> 00:03:48.428
if they were indicted. Right. Exactly.

00:03:48.461 --> 00:03:48.828
But there are,

00:03:48.828 --> 00:03:49.162
of course,

00:03:49.162 --> 00:03:50.697
extraordinary circumstances here

00:03:50.697 --> 00:03:52.832
because he has Secret Service protection.

00:03:52.832 --> 00:03:55.435
There are significant security concerns.

00:03:55.435 --> 00:03:57.003
You can see right there behind Kara.

00:03:57.003 --> 00:03:57.270
I mean,

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:59.038
this is a very crowded area

00:03:59.038 --> 00:04:00.240
of downtown Manhattan.

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:01.007
That courthouse

00:04:01.007 --> 00:04:02.609
is a circus on a good day.

00:04:02.609 --> 00:04:04.310
So there are absolutely security

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:05.178
concerns here.

00:04:05.178 --> 00:04:05.912
But politically,

00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:06.613
it appears a former

00:04:06.613 --> 00:04:08.281
president wants to lean into this,

00:04:08.281 --> 00:04:10.149
wants to appear in person

00:04:10.149 --> 00:04:11.451
and really make a thing out of this,

00:04:11.451 --> 00:04:12.552
because he believes

00:04:12.552 --> 00:04:13.653
that politically

00:04:13.653 --> 00:04:15.688
this indictment could help him.

00:04:15.688 --> 00:04:17.223
It's truly a major development

00:04:17.223 --> 00:04:18.925
unfolding in New York right now.

00:04:18.925 --> 00:04:20.760
Let me get Gloria Borger into this.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:22.495
Gloria, what do you think?

00:04:22.495 --> 00:04:24.664
Well, I think this is historic.

00:04:24.797 --> 00:04:26.766
I think we've never seen

00:04:26.766 --> 00:04:29.035
a former president be indicted before.

00:04:29.469 --> 00:04:32.272
And I think that while the circumstances

00:04:32.272 --> 00:04:33.439
of this case, as we all

00:04:33.439 --> 00:04:36.409
know, are a bit tawdry and in some,

00:04:36.476 --> 00:04:37.377
particularly in the legal

00:04:37.377 --> 00:04:38.311
profession, are saying,

00:04:38.311 --> 00:04:39.612
look, it's not as important

00:04:39.612 --> 00:04:40.546
what might as

00:04:40.546 --> 00:04:42.582
what might be coming down the pike

00:04:42.582 --> 00:04:44.083
in terms of the Atlanta

00:04:44.083 --> 00:04:45.018
grand jury

00:04:45.018 --> 00:04:46.519
and election interference

00:04:46.519 --> 00:04:48.855
and in terms of the documents at Mar

00:04:48.855 --> 00:04:50.023
a Lago.

00:04:50.023 --> 00:04:51.224
This nonetheless,

00:04:51.224 --> 00:04:51.924
an indictment

00:04:51.924 --> 00:04:53.226
is something that Donald Trump

00:04:53.226 --> 00:04:55.261
has evaded for years and years.

00:04:55.361 --> 00:04:57.530
And it would be the first time

00:04:57.897 --> 00:04:59.265
and I think it is something

00:04:59.265 --> 00:05:02.101
that Donald Trump clearly intends to use

00:05:02.802 --> 00:05:03.770
to his benefit,

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:06.372
at least with his base early on

00:05:06.372 --> 00:05:08.274
in this election season.

00:05:08.274 --> 00:05:09.075
But we're going to have

00:05:09.075 --> 00:05:11.944
to watch this play out before our eyes

00:05:12.345 --> 00:05:14.881
as he has to be booked and charged.

00:05:15.181 --> 00:05:16.416
And I think that

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:18.551
I think that's going

00:05:18.551 --> 00:05:19.052
to be

00:05:19.052 --> 00:05:21.254
remarkable for the American public

00:05:21.454 --> 00:05:22.322
to see.

00:05:22.322 --> 00:05:23.222
People are going to have different

00:05:23.222 --> 00:05:24.357
interpretations of it.

00:05:24.357 --> 00:05:25.258
He's going to claim

00:05:25.258 --> 00:05:27.327
he's the victim, etc., etc..

00:05:27.327 --> 00:05:28.695
We need to look at the indictment.

00:05:28.695 --> 00:05:30.763
We need to look at what it says.

00:05:30.763 --> 00:05:32.832
But it is a moment in history, Wolf.

00:05:32.832 --> 00:05:34.000
It certainly is a very,

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:36.502
very dramatic and historic moment indeed.

00:05:36.869 --> 00:05:38.338
Kaitlan Collins has covered Trump

00:05:38.338 --> 00:05:40.473
for several years now. She's joining us.

00:05:40.473 --> 00:05:42.175
What else are you learning, Caitlin?

00:05:42.175 --> 00:05:43.476
Wolf, I mean, the president's

00:05:43.476 --> 00:05:45.044
legal team had been bracing for this.

00:05:45.044 --> 00:05:45.311
The former

00:05:45.311 --> 00:05:46.212
president's legal team,

00:05:46.212 --> 00:05:47.513
they knew that this was likely

00:05:47.513 --> 00:05:48.481
something that could happen.

00:05:48.481 --> 00:05:49.282
He himself,

00:05:49.282 --> 00:05:50.583
of course, has been bracing for it

00:05:50.583 --> 00:05:51.284
ever since.

00:05:51.284 --> 00:05:53.152
He said that he believed last Tuesday

00:05:53.152 --> 00:05:55.021
he was going to potentially be arrested.

00:05:55.021 --> 00:05:56.489
Obviously, it did not happen.

00:05:56.489 --> 00:05:57.190
At that time,

00:05:57.190 --> 00:05:58.858
they didn't really have a window

00:05:58.858 --> 00:06:00.426
into what the timing here

00:06:00.426 --> 00:06:01.594
was going to look like.

00:06:01.594 --> 00:06:03.129
They obviously were operating

00:06:03.129 --> 00:06:04.130
under what we had

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:05.932
heard as of yesterday, which was that

00:06:05.932 --> 00:06:06.632
there was potentially

00:06:06.632 --> 00:06:09.535
going to be a hiatus for this grand jury.

00:06:09.535 --> 00:06:11.337
But now, obviously, this has happened.

00:06:11.337 --> 00:06:13.373
And so the question is what happens next?

00:06:13.373 --> 00:06:14.674
Because his attorneys have said

00:06:14.674 --> 00:06:16.042
that he will surrender,

00:06:16.042 --> 00:06:17.677
that he will fly his plane here

00:06:17.677 --> 00:06:19.645
to New York to go through the next steps

00:06:19.645 --> 00:06:20.780
where he's going to be

00:06:20.780 --> 00:06:22.715
fingerprinted and photographed

00:06:22.715 --> 00:06:23.516
for the next steps

00:06:23.516 --> 00:06:25.318
of what an indictment looks like.

00:06:25.318 --> 00:06:26.986
We don't know how soon that will happen.

00:06:26.986 --> 00:06:28.521
It could take several days.

00:06:28.521 --> 00:06:30.990
But they have been planning to do a very

00:06:31.958 --> 00:06:32.759
delicate,

00:06:32.759 --> 00:06:33.659
intricate detail, I

00:06:33.659 --> 00:06:35.161
should note level of what

00:06:35.161 --> 00:06:35.828
that is going

00:06:35.828 --> 00:06:36.929
to look like, talking

00:06:36.929 --> 00:06:38.965
about the kind of facial expression

00:06:38.965 --> 00:06:39.632
he has as he's

00:06:39.632 --> 00:06:40.900
walking into the courthouse,

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:42.568
if it is in front of the cameras

00:06:42.568 --> 00:06:43.236
as typically

00:06:43.236 --> 00:06:45.037
is the case here in Manhattan,

00:06:45.037 --> 00:06:46.005
because they know

00:06:46.005 --> 00:06:47.273
that that is going to be an image

00:06:47.273 --> 00:06:49.075
that is broadcast around the world.

00:06:49.075 --> 00:06:50.343
They know it's going to be something

00:06:50.343 --> 00:06:52.044
they believe, as Paula was saying

00:06:52.044 --> 00:06:53.413
to his political advantage

00:06:53.413 --> 00:06:55.014
that he can use as he is running

00:06:55.014 --> 00:06:56.816
this third campaign for president.

00:06:56.816 --> 00:06:58.818
But I think we have heard this refrain

00:06:58.818 --> 00:07:00.420
from some people in recent days

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:01.053
that say

00:07:01.053 --> 00:07:02.655
he actually wants to be indicted.

00:07:02.655 --> 00:07:03.723
They think it will be good for him.

00:07:03.723 --> 00:07:05.691
He does not want to be indicted,

00:07:05.691 --> 00:07:07.326
certainly not for this case.

00:07:07.326 --> 00:07:08.761
This is one of the most personally

00:07:08.761 --> 00:07:10.496
sensitive situations for him.

00:07:10.496 --> 00:07:11.230
It was ever

00:07:11.230 --> 00:07:12.899
when he was in the White House.

00:07:12.899 --> 00:07:13.800
There was reporting on this

00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:14.700
on a daily basis

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:15.935
on who made these payments

00:07:15.935 --> 00:07:17.537
and who knew about these payments,

00:07:17.537 --> 00:07:19.105
because it involves allegations

00:07:19.105 --> 00:07:19.872
about an affair.

00:07:19.872 --> 00:07:20.573
And it was something

00:07:20.573 --> 00:07:22.275
that greatly bothered

00:07:22.275 --> 00:07:22.975
the first lady,

00:07:22.975 --> 00:07:24.343
Melania Trump, at the time.

00:07:24.343 --> 00:07:26.446
And so it is a very sensitive case

00:07:26.446 --> 00:07:27.480
actually for Trump.

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:28.347
And I think the idea

00:07:28.347 --> 00:07:29.749
that he wanted to be indicted

00:07:29.749 --> 00:07:30.483
does not match

00:07:30.483 --> 00:07:32.518
with any of the reporting that I've had.

00:07:32.518 --> 00:07:33.886
But it is a historic nature

00:07:33.886 --> 00:07:35.388
that he is now the first U.S.

00:07:35.388 --> 00:07:36.422
president, former U.S.

00:07:36.422 --> 00:07:38.524
president, to face criminal charges.

00:07:38.558 --> 00:07:38.891
Yeah, it's

00:07:38.891 --> 00:07:40.593
really a dramatic moment indeed.

00:07:40.593 --> 00:07:41.294
Kristen Holmes,

00:07:41.294 --> 00:07:42.562
our national correspondent,

00:07:42.562 --> 00:07:44.430
is also working her stories,

00:07:44.430 --> 00:07:45.631
her sources for us.

00:07:45.631 --> 00:07:47.133
What else are you learning, Kristen?

00:07:47.133 --> 00:07:47.867
Yeah, I've just heard

00:07:47.867 --> 00:07:48.868
from a number of members

00:07:48.868 --> 00:07:49.936
of Trump's inner circle

00:07:49.936 --> 00:07:51.938
who are all trying to figure out

00:07:51.938 --> 00:07:52.972
exactly what's going on.

00:07:52.972 --> 00:07:54.173
As Paula said,

00:07:54.173 --> 00:07:55.741
they have not yet heard

00:07:55.741 --> 00:07:56.642
from their attorneys.

00:07:56.642 --> 00:07:58.211
They have not gotten the information yet

00:07:58.211 --> 00:07:59.278
in order to proceed.

00:07:59.278 --> 00:07:59.912
But we are waiting

00:07:59.912 --> 00:08:01.280
for a statement on that.

00:08:01.280 --> 00:08:02.315
And I do want to talk about what

00:08:02.315 --> 00:08:03.516
Caitlin just mentioned,

00:08:03.516 --> 00:08:05.451
which is this intricate detail

00:08:05.451 --> 00:08:06.486
of what it looks like

00:08:06.486 --> 00:08:09.188
to bring Donald Trump to the courthouse.

00:08:09.422 --> 00:08:12.258
They are looking at how exactly

00:08:12.258 --> 00:08:13.926
this is going to play out.

00:08:13.926 --> 00:08:16.062
There is a huge security component.

00:08:16.262 --> 00:08:18.498
There is also a optics component.

00:08:18.531 --> 00:08:19.999
They are talking about, as Caitlin said,

00:08:19.999 --> 00:08:20.900
facial expressions.

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:21.968
They're also talking about

00:08:21.968 --> 00:08:23.703
when is he going to make a statement?

00:08:23.703 --> 00:08:24.370
Who is he going

00:08:24.370 --> 00:08:25.638
to make that statement to?

00:08:25.638 --> 00:08:27.440
Where is that going to be?

00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:28.975
And, you know, last week

00:08:28.975 --> 00:08:30.343
we reported that in the heat

00:08:30.343 --> 00:08:31.344
of all of this,

00:08:31.344 --> 00:08:31.744
that Trump

00:08:31.744 --> 00:08:33.479
had really run the gamut of emotions

00:08:33.479 --> 00:08:35.481
and he had sort of resigned himself

00:08:35.648 --> 00:08:36.516
to the fact

00:08:36.516 --> 00:08:38.784
that he was likely to get indicted.

00:08:38.818 --> 00:08:39.151
However,

00:08:39.151 --> 00:08:41.554
some of that did shift in recent days.

00:08:41.554 --> 00:08:42.021
I talked to

00:08:42.021 --> 00:08:43.489
some people who are close to

00:08:43.489 --> 00:08:45.157
Trump, would talk to the former president

00:08:45.157 --> 00:08:45.458
who said

00:08:45.458 --> 00:08:47.426
because of the fact that the grand jury

00:08:47.426 --> 00:08:49.262
wasn't meeting because of this reporting,

00:08:49.262 --> 00:08:50.463
that they were hearing another case,

00:08:50.463 --> 00:08:51.764
because all of that came

00:08:51.764 --> 00:08:52.932
after Costello's

00:08:52.932 --> 00:08:54.567
testimony in front of the grand jury.

00:08:54.567 --> 00:08:56.502
There were some hope there

00:08:56.502 --> 00:08:58.337
that maybe this meant this wasn't

00:08:58.337 --> 00:08:59.305
going to happen.

00:08:59.305 --> 00:08:59.805
And again,

00:08:59.805 --> 00:09:00.573
as Caitlin said,

00:09:00.573 --> 00:09:02.108
this is not something

00:09:02.108 --> 00:09:03.643
that the former president wants.

00:09:03.643 --> 00:09:06.546
And even though we hear spin all the time

00:09:06.712 --> 00:09:07.680
from Republicans,

00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:08.915
from the former president himself,

00:09:08.915 --> 00:09:09.382
who says that

00:09:09.382 --> 00:09:11.250
this is going to help him politically,

00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:13.486
which it does appear in some cases

00:09:13.486 --> 00:09:15.621
it might in a contested primary.

00:09:15.621 --> 00:09:17.223
There are still a lot of Trump

00:09:17.223 --> 00:09:18.624
allies and advisers,

00:09:18.624 --> 00:09:19.725
people who are close to him,

00:09:19.725 --> 00:09:21.594
who want him to win the nomination

00:09:21.594 --> 00:09:23.563
and the presidency in 2024,

00:09:23.563 --> 00:09:24.330
who don't think that

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:25.898
this will help him in the long run,

00:09:25.898 --> 00:09:27.967
or at least are very concerned

00:09:28.167 --> 00:09:29.268
about what this is going to do

00:09:29.268 --> 00:09:30.870
with his political career Wolf.

00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:31.904
Yeah, it's clear.

00:09:31.904 --> 00:09:32.438
Go ahead.

00:09:32.438 --> 00:09:32.672
Well,

00:09:32.672 --> 00:09:34.740
let me just add that I've just heard that

00:09:35.641 --> 00:09:36.976
not only was the president

00:09:36.976 --> 00:09:37.710
not informed us,

00:09:37.710 --> 00:09:39.211
as you guys were reporting,

00:09:39.211 --> 00:09:40.146
but also Michael

00:09:40.146 --> 00:09:40.780
Cohen's team

00:09:40.780 --> 00:09:43.249
was not informed of this in advance.

00:09:44.150 --> 00:09:45.284
And so I think

00:09:45.284 --> 00:09:46.552
everyone's been kind of kept in the

00:09:46.552 --> 00:09:47.853
dark on both sides of this.

